## STEP 6/7 — COMPLETE

The reference matrix-vector path now uses real mmap-backed Qwen weights and supports the required Q5_0 and Q8_0 tensor formats through scalar F32 dequantization. A model-level TensorView accessor resolves exact names and preserves the mapped file as the source of truth.

For the real `Hello` prompt, token ID `9707` was embedded and RMS-normalized, then projected through layer 0 using the real tensors:

```text
blk.0.attn_q.weight: Q5_0, 896 x 896
blk.0.attn_k.weight: Q5_0, 896 x 128
blk.0.attn_v.weight: Q8_0, 896 x 128
```

The first eight Q/K/V values were independently recomputed by a scalar Python decoder. Maximum absolute differences against the C++ printed values were:

```text
Q: 4.92e-06 (printed-value comparison)
K: 4.92e-07 (printed-value comparison)
V: 3.78e-08 (printed-value comparison)
```

The larger Q difference is explained by the C++ probe printing only six significant decimal digits; the independent values agree at the displayed precision. The implementation itself and the independent decoder use the same exact GGUF block layout, so a future full-precision comparison harness should compare binary/serialized vectors rather than rounded console output.

